# RuneScape Loot Filter (.rs2f) — Agent Reference

## Project Structure
- **config.rs2f** — Main config: global settings, `#define` variables, applies all modules
- **modules/filtering/** — Item filtering rules by category (bars, gems, ores, logs, runes, food, potions, herbs, currency, farming_seeds, fishing, ammo, clue_scrolls, metal_equipment, ownership, value_based)
- **modules/individual_item_styles/** — Per-item styling for specific categories
- **modules/item_category_styles/** — Bulk styling per skill/activity (construction, farming, fishing, fletching, herblore, mining, prayer, smithing, woodcutting, etc.)
- Each directory contains `_module_definition.rs2f` defining module structure and UI options

---

## File Structure & Syntax

```rs2f
meta { name = "author/filter"; description = "..."; }  // REQUIRED; name must be unique

#define VAR_NAME value          // user-configurable (VAR_ prefix) or constant (CONST_ prefix)

apply (condition) { prop=val; }  // non-terminal: applies settings, continues evaluating
rule (condition) { prop=val; }   // terminal: stops evaluation on match
```

### Module & Input UI Annotations
Structured comments for the filterscape UI. Place between `meta{}` and `#define` blocks:

```rs2f
/*@ define:module:[id]
name: Display Name
subtitle: Short phrase
description: |
    Markdown-supported description
*/

/*@ define:input:module_id
type: boolean|number|stringlist|enumlist|style
label: UI Label
*/
#define VAR_X default_value   // input comment MUST sit directly above #define
```

| Input Type | Description | Example Default |
|-----------|-------------|-----------------|
| `boolean` | Checkbox toggle | `#define VAR_X true` |
| `number` | Integer input | `#define VAR_X 100` |
| `stringlist` | Free-form string array | `#define VAR_X ["item"]` |
| `enumlist` | Dropdown (value/label pairs) | `#define VAR_X ["option"]` |
| `style` | Visual settings (colors in `#AARRGGBB`) | `#define VAR_X textColor="#FFFFFFFF"` |

---

## Conditions

### Syntax: `<type>:<operator><value>`

| Type | Syntax | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| `id` | `id:<n>`, `id:[n,n]` | Exact item ID(s) |
| `name` | `name:"str"`, `name:["a","b"]` | Case-insensitive, wildcard `*` on either/both sides |
| `quantity` | `quantity:<op><n>` | |
| `value` | `value:<op><n>` | Highest of GE vs HA value |
| `gevalue` | `gevalue:<op><n>` | GE price only |
| `havalue` | `havalue:<op><n>` | High alchemy only |
| `tradeable` | `tradeable:<bool>` | |
| `stackable` | `stackable:<bool>` | |
| `noted` | `noted:<bool>` | |
| `ownership` | `ownership:<n>` | 0=none, 1=self, 2=other, 3=group |
| `area` | `area:[x0,y0,z0,x1,y1,z1]` | World coordinate bounding box |

### Operators
- Comparison: `==`, `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=` — **NO `!=`**, use `!` prefix: `!quantity:==1`
- Logical: `&&`, `||`, `!` — precedence: `&&` > `||`; use parentheses for control

### Examples
```rs2f
name:"coins" && quantity:>100_000
!quantity:==1                    // quantity != 1
(name:"blue dragonhide" || name:"green dragonhide") && value:>500
```

---

## Display Settings

Set inside `{ }`, **semicolon-terminated**. Defaults noted where applicable.

### Visibility & Overlay
| Setting | Type | Description |
|---------|------|-------------|
| `hidden` | bool | Hides everything (no lootbeam, no tile highlight) |
| `hideOverlay` | bool | Hides text overlay only |
| `showValue` | bool | Show item value in overlay |
| `showDespawn` | bool | Show despawn timer |

### Text Styling
| Setting | Type | Description |
|---------|------|-------------|
| `color`, `textColor` | color string | Text color |
| `backgroundColor` | color string | Background behind text |
| `borderColor` | color string | Border around text |
| `fontType` | enum | `FONTTYPE_SMALL`(1, default), `FONTTYPE_NORMAL`(2), `FONTTYPE_BOLD`(3) |
| `textAccent` | enum | `TEXTACCENT_SHADOW`(1, default), `TEXTACCENT_OUTLINE`(2), `TEXTACCENT_NONE`(3), `TEXTACCENT_BOLD_SHADOW`(4) |
| `textAccentColor` | color string | Accent/shadow color (default: black) |
| `menuTextColor` | color string | Menu entry text color (defaults to textColor) |

### Lootbeam
| Setting | Type | Description |
|---------|------|-------------|
| `showLootbeam`, `showLootBeam` | bool | Show in-world lootbeam |
| `lootbeamColor`, `lootBeamColor` | color string | Beam color (defaults to textColor) |

### Tile Highlighting
| Setting | Type | Description |
|---------|------|-------------|
| `highlightTile` | bool | Highlight item's ground tile |
| `tileStrokeColor` | color string | Tile outline color (defaults to textColor) |
| `tileFillColor` | color string | Tile fill color (no fill when unset) |

### Notifications & Audio
| Setting | Type | Description |
|---------|------|-------------|
| `notify` | bool | Fire system notification on drop |
| `sound` | int or string | Sound ID from game cache, OR filename from `.runelite/loot-filters/sounds/` (WAV recommended) |

### Icons
```rs2f
icon = Sprite(index, imageIndex)   // Game sprite — browse: https://abextm.github.io/cache2/#/viewer/sprite
icon = Item(itemId)                // Item icon by ID
icon = File("name.png")            // Custom from .runelite/loot-filters/icons/ (PNG recommended)
icon = CurrentItem()               // Item's own icon
```

### Menu Sorting
| Setting | Type | Description |
|---------|------|-------------|
| `menuSort` | int | Pickup menu order. Higher = higher priority. Negative values supported. |

---

## Colors & Macros

### Color Formats (all equivalent)
`"#rrggbb"`, `"#aarrggbb"`, `"rrggbb"`, `"aarrggbb"` — 8-digit `#AARRGGBB` preferred for UI inputs.

### Macros (`#define`)
```rs2f
#define ORANGE "#ffa500"

// Multi-line (backslash continuation)
#define IMPORTANT(_name, _color) rule (name:_name) {\
  color = _color; \
  notify = true;\
}
IMPORTANT("twisted bow", GREEN)
```

---

## Complete Example

```rs2f
meta { name = "riktenx/test"; description = "demo filter"; }

/*@ define:module:my_module
name: My Module
subtitle: Filtering controls
description: |
    Configure item visibility and styling
*/

/*@ define:input:my_module
type: stringlist
label: Items To Hide
*/
#define VAR_ITEMS_TO_HIDE ["ashes"]

apply (value:>10_000) { borderColor = "#ff80ff"; }   // non-terminal: stacks
rule (name:"anglerfish") { color = MAGENTA; }         // terminal: stops here
rule (name:"coins") { color = YELLOW; showLootbeam = true; }

if (name:VAR_ITEMS_TO_HIDE) {
    hidden = true;
}
```

---

## Agent Rules

1. **Always include `meta` block** with a unique `name`
2. **Top-down evaluation** — order matters, first matching `rule` wins
3. **`apply` for stacking**, `rule` for final decisions
4. **No nested rules** — flatten: `rule (a && b) { ... }`
5. **Semicolons required** after display settings; whitespace is flexible
6. **Numeric literals support underscores:** `100_000` = 100000
7. **No `!=` operator** — use negation: `!quantity:==1`
8. **Input comments MUST sit directly above** their `#define` (default value is pulled from it)
9. **Naming conventions:** `VAR_` prefix for configurable, `CONST_` for constants
10. **New rules go in appropriate module files**; prefer user-configurable settings with UI annotations
11. **Preserve existing functionality** unless explicitly asked to change
